---
/**
 * Loads the Altitude element registry so the generated playgrounds upgrade.
 *
 * A per-page deep import (`al-web-components/components/<slug>`) would be
 * leaner, but the tag a detail page needs is only known at build time and a
 * bare-specifier dynamic import is not statically analyzable by Vite — so the
 * docs site pays one bundle and guarantees every one of the generated
 * playgrounds actually renders a real custom element rather than an
 * un-upgraded tag.
 *
 * Requires `window.alAutoRegistry = true` inline in <head> (Shell.astro) —
 * the deep modules read it at module-eval time to decide whether to call
 * `customElements.define` (see .altitude/REGISTRATION.md).
 */
---

<script>
  import 'al-web-components';
</script>
